DAY MODE:

colorPallette{
    Dark Blue: rgb(10, 39, 78) - Used for the text and the wave icon details.

Off-White: rgb(255, 255, 255) - Used for the main background.

Embossed Blue: RGB (16, 49, 90) - Used for the background and embossed waves on the left.
} */



Night Mode Color Pallette:
To create a professional night mode for this design, you want to avoid pure black. Because "Bay Breeze" has a coastal, water-based identity, using deep, desaturated slate-blues will make the dark mode feel cohesive with your brand while reducing eye strain.

Here is a balanced, high-contrast dark mode palette:

Main Page Background: #0F172A (Deep Slate)

Why: A rich, very dark blue-gray that acts as a softer alternative to stark black.

Card Background: #1E293B (Elevated Slate)

Why: Slightly lighter than the background to make the card "pop" forward and maintain that structural layout without using borders.

Main Text: #F1F5F9 (Crisp Off-White)

Why: Pure white on dark backgrounds can cause glare. This soft white ensures high readability.

Header / Nav Bar: rgb(10, 39, 78) (Your Original Navy)

Why: You can actually keep your current header color! It will blend beautifully into the deep slate body background while anchoring your brand identity.

The "+" Button (Accent): #38BDF8 (Vibrant Light Blue)

Why: Since your dark navy button will disappear into a dark card, shifting it to a bright, energetic light blue provides excellent contrast and draws the user's eye exactly where they need to click.